灯奇怪的闪烁归因于Alice公主，
the strange flickering light to Princess Alice,

693
00:34:16,200 --> 00:34:17,920
但他们不能理解
but they cannot comprehend

694
00:34:18,030 --> 00:34:20,960
她正在向他们传达信息。
that she's doing it to send them a message.

695
00:34:21,070 --> 00:34:23,630
尽管更小的孩子也会向神祈祷，
And while younger kids might pray to God,

696
00:34:23,740 --> 00:34:26,030
但Jesse的研究表明
Jesse's work shows

697
00:34:26,140 --> 00:34:30,130
只有大一点的、具有更高智力成长的孩子
that only older children with more developed intelligence

698
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:33,000
才能确切体会到神
actually perceive answers to prayers

699
00:34:33,110 --> 00:34:34,940
对他们祈祷的回应。
in the world around them.

700
00:34:35,050 --> 00:34:37,780
Alice公主代表了一类神灵。
Princess Alice is basically being sort of a God by proxy.

701
00:34:37,890 --> 00:34:39,450
她使得
She's making these happen

702
00:34:39,560 --> 00:34:41,780
像灯闪烁的现象
like the light flashing on and off

703
00:34:41,890 --> 00:34:45,120
就像上帝创造了雷雨
just like God would, in principle, create a thunderstorm

704
00:34:45,230 --> 00:34:46,550
是在传递某个信息
to give one a message

705
00:34:46,670 --> 00:34:50,490
或是在停车场恰好出现了一个车位。
or create a parking lot opening up at just the right time.

706
00:34:50,600 --> 00:34:53,120
Jesse认为
Jesse believes

707
00:34:53,240 --> 00:34:56,590
我们发展出了可以读到这些信息的精神能力，
we develop the mental ability to read these messages

708
00:34:56,710 --> 00:34:58,960
不论我们是否信仰上帝。
whether we believe in God or not.

709
00:34:59,080 --> 00:35:02,200
Jesse第一次体会到这种现象
Jesse experienced this phenomenon firsthand

710
00:35:02,310 --> 00:35:03,930
在他母亲，Alice，
when his mother, Alice,

711
00:35:04,050 --> 00:35:06,400
就是Alice公主的灵感来源，
the inspiration behind Princess Alice,

712
00:35:06,520 --> 00:35:08,010
去世的时候。
was dying.

713
00:35:08,120 --> 00:35:09,670
她完全不相信
She wasn't convinced absolutely

714
00:35:09,790 --> 00:35:11,310
死后还会有什么，
that there was something after death,

715
00:35:11,420 --> 00:35:12,810
但她告诉我如果真的有，
but she told me that if there was,

716
00:35:12,920 --> 00:35:13,980
她无论如何都会回来
she would come back somehow

717
00:35:14,090 --> 00:35:15,850
给我带来信息，和我交流。
and give me a message and communicate with me.

718
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:17,710
她去世后，
After she passed,

719
00:35:17,830 --> 00:35:20,250
Jesse心中充满悲伤，
Jesse was overwhelmed with grief,

720
00:35:20,360 --> 00:35:21,920
作为一名科学家，
and as a scientist,

721
00:35:22,030 --> 00:35:25,150
他对自己下一步的想法感到震惊。
he was shocked at what his mind did next.

722
00:35:25,270 --> 00:35:27,990
当她去世后的第二天晚上，
When she died, the following evening,

723
00:35:28,100 --> 00:35:31,690
她去世时窗外的风铃
the wind chimes outside of her window where she had passed away

724
00:35:31,810 --> 00:35:33,940
开始晃动，发出声音...
started to move and make sound...

725
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:38,900
很奇怪的是当时并没有很大的风，
...which was odd because there wasn't a lot of wind,

726
00:35:39,010 --> 00:35:41,630
我的思维马上得到结论：
and my mind immediately sort of leapt to the conclusion

727
00:35:41,750 --> 00:35:44,300
这是我母亲在告诉我她很好。
that this was my mother telling me that she was okay.

728
00:35:44,420 --> 00:35:46,910
她在向我传达消息，告诉我不要担心她，
She was giving me a message not to worry about her,

729
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:49,150
一切都很好。
everything was fine.

730
00:35:50,890 --> 00:35:52,080
这完全是无意识的。
It's completely unconscious.

731
00:35:52,190 --> 00:35:54,250
这不是我努力思考得到的结果。
It's not something deliberate that I was trying to do.

732
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,990
就这么发生的。
It just happened.

733
00:35:57,730 --> 00:36:01,220
信仰是人类认知系统的
Belief is basically sort of the default setting

734
00:36:01,330 --> 00:36:03,550
一类默认设置。
for the human cognitive system.

735
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:07,960
它使得我们具有强大的直觉
It's seducing us with these very powerful intuitions

736
00:36:08,070 --> 00:36:10,540
认为事出有因。
that things happen for a reason.

737
00:36:16,810 --> 00:36:18,860
Jesse的工作表明
Jesse's work shows

738
00:36:18,980 --> 00:36:21,570
我们都自然而然的发展出了
we all naturally develop the ability

739
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:24,640
从神那里接受信息的能力。
to receive messages from God.

740
00:36:24,750 --> 00:36:28,810
信仰者认为感受到的信息是真实的。
Believers feel these messages are real.

741
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:32,710
无神论者认为这些只是我们的想象。
Atheists argue they are just in our imagination.

742
00:36:32,820 --> 00:36:37,650
而这位神经学家正在窥察我们的思维，
And this neuroscientist is peering into our minds,

743
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:41,190
试图发现谁才是对的。
trying to discover who is right.

744
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:46,460
什么才是真的？
What is real?

745
00:36:46,570 --> 00:36:48,460
我们通过
We define reality

746
00:36:48,570 --> 00:36:54,570
看、听、触、闻或尝定义现实。
by what we can see, hear, touch, smell, or taste.

747
00:36:54,740 --> 00:36:56,330
在大脑中，
Inside the brain,

748
00:36:56,440 --> 00:36:59,930
这些感觉以电信号形式存在。
these senses exist as electrical signals.

749
00:37:00,620 --> 00:37:04,610
对于我们来说，现实的总体
For us, the entire sum of all reality

750
00:37:04,730 --> 00:37:09,720
就储存在“电缆束”中。
is contained in this bundle of electrical wiring.

751
00:37:09,830 --> 00:37:13,970
那当我们的大脑感受到神...
So, when our brains sense God...

752
00:37:16,170 --> 00:37:20,500
...就认为这神是真实的？
...does that make God real?

753
00:37:20,610 --> 00:37:26,330
Andy Newberg是神经神学的创始人，
Andy Newberg is the founding father of Neurotheology,

754
00:37:26,450 --> 00:37:28,240
神经科学的一个新分支
a new branch of neuroscience

755
00:37:28,350 --> 00:37:32,240
主要研究人类大脑的灵性作用。
that studies the effects of spirituality on the human brain.

756
00:37:32,350 --> 00:37:35,380
这个科学问题，
It's a scientific quest he has pursued

757
00:37:35,490 --> 00:37:37,480
从他记事起就开始追寻答案。
as long as he can remember.

758
00:37:37,590 --> 00:37:39,040
还是个小孩的时候，
Ever since I was a kid,

759
00:37:39,160 --> 00:37:42,580
我就对理解现实非常感兴趣。
I was very interested in trying to understand reality.

760
00:37:42,690 --> 00:37:44,180
我感到很困扰，
I was disturbed by the fact

761
00:37:44,300 --> 00:37:46,680
因为每个人都看的是同样的现实，
that everyone was looking at the same reality,

762
00:37:46,800 --> 00:37:48,450
可还是有不同的宗教
and yet there were people with different religions

763
00:37:48,570 --> 00:37:50,390
和不同的政治信仰。
and different political beliefs.

764
00:37:50,500 --> 00:37:52,460
Andy找到了一种方法
Andy found a way

765
00:37:52,570 --> 00:37:54,960
可以看到信仰者
to peer inside the brains of believers

766
00:37:55,070 --> 00:37:58,230
在宗教仪式中的大脑。
while they were in the midst of a religious ritual.

767
00:37:58,340 --> 00:38:02,900
这是最高端的大脑成像设备--
It's the highest of high-tech brain-imaging devices --

768
00:38:03,010 --> 00:38:05,000
SPECT扫描仪。
the SPECT scanner.

769
00:38:05,110 --> 00:38:06,500
我会进去，
I'm gonna come in,

770
00:38:06,610 --> 00:38:08,670
然后会用一种金质物质输入到你体内，
and I'm gonna just inject you through the I.V. with the gold,

771
00:38:08,780 --> 00:38:10,410
我会尽量不打扰你
and I'm gonna try very hard not to disturb you

772
00:38:10,520 --> 00:38:12,510
不让你分心或制造噪声，
or distract you or make any noise,

773
00:38:12,620 --> 00:38:16,280
你只需要继续你的祷告就行，
and you're just gonna continue to do your prayer session

774
00:38:16,390 --> 00:38:17,480
直到祷告结束。
until it's done.

775
00:38:17,590 --> 00:38:20,920
这位女士是名长老会牧师。
This woman is a Presbyterian minister.

776
00:38:21,030 --> 00:38:24,820
她每天向上帝祷告，已经超过34年。
She's prayed to God daily for over 34 years.

777
00:38:24,930 --> 00:38:28,960
现在，她专注于祷告。
Right now, she's deep in prayer.

778
00:38:29,070 --> 00:38:31,630
在她与上帝联系的峰值时期，
At the height of her connection with God,

779
00:38:31,740 --> 00:38:36,010
Andy向她注射了一种无害的放射性染料。
Andy injects her with a harmless radioactive dye.

780
00:38:38,280 --> 00:38:40,740
接下来的几分钟，
Over the course of the next few minutes

781
00:38:40,850 --> 00:38:42,340
她继续祷告，
as she continues to pray,

782
00:38:42,450 --> 00:38:45,080
染料移动到她大脑部分
the dye migrates to the parts of her brain

783
00:38:45,190 --> 00:38:47,950
这里她的血流最强。
where the blood flow is the strongest.

784
00:38:48,060 --> 00:38:49,780
大脑工作很好
The brain works in a very nice way

785
00:38:49,890 --> 00:38:51,520
某个特定区域活性越强，
that the more active a particular part is,

786
00:38:51,630 --> 00:38:52,880
血流就越多，
the more blood flow it gets,

787
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:55,550
活性越低，那里的血流就越少。
and the less active it is, the less blood flow it gets.

788
00:38:55,670 --> 00:38:59,260
这些是她的大脑图像
These are the images of her brain

789
00:38:59,370 --> 00:39:01,720
分别在祷告之前和祷告中。
before and during her prayer.

790
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:03,360
颜色越红，
The redder the shade,

791
00:39:03,470 --> 00:39:06,400
就表示这里的神经区域活性越高。
the more active the neural area is.

792
00:39:06,510 --> 00:39:08,260
这是静息时扫描结果。
This is the resting scan.

793
00:39:08,380 --> 00:39:09,830
这是祷告时扫描结果，
This is the prayer scan

794
00:39:09,950 --> 00:39:13,000
表现出了大脑额叶活性
showing increased activity in the frontal lobes

795
00:39:13,120 --> 00:39:16,010
和语言区域活性的增强。
and in the language area of the brain.

796
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:19,240
Andy扫描了上百个
Andy has scanned hundreds of brains

797
00:39:19,350 --> 00:39:22,480
在祈祷中的大脑，
in the midst of their prayer rituals,

798
00:39:22,590 --> 00:39:25,480
从穆斯林阿訇到藏族僧侣
from Muslim imams to Tibetan monks

799
00:39:25,590 --> 00:39:28,150
以及冥想无神论者。
to meditating atheists.

800
00:39:39,300 --> 00:39:43,190
在我们进行交谈时活性激增。
is intensely active when we hold conversations.

801
00:41:24,620 --> 00:41:26,640
所有的宗教都创造了一种神经体验
that all religions create neurological experiences

802
00:41:26,750 --> 00:41:28,510
就像神真正
that are just as real

803
00:41:28,620 --> 00:41:34,150
存在于我们大脑之外的世界一样。
as if God physically existed in the world outside our brains.

804
00:41:34,260 --> 00:41:37,320
如果神仅存在于我们的大脑中，
And if God only exists inside our brains,

805
00:41:37,430 --> 00:41:40,120
这也并不意味着神不是真的。
that does not mean God is not real.

806
00:41:40,230 --> 00:41:45,800
我们的大脑是我们对现实认识的结晶。
Our brains are where reality crystallizes for us.

807
00:41:47,610 --> 00:41:49,430
显然这种概念
There's certainly this notion

808
00:41:49,540 --> 00:41:51,860
有大过我们所有人的东西存在，
that there is something bigger than all of us here,

809
00:41:51,980 --> 00:41:53,530
这是否是整个宇宙
and whether it's the whole universe

810
00:41:53,640 --> 00:41:55,770
或是是否有超越所有的存在，
or whether there is something beyond all of that,

811
00:41:55,880 --> 00:41:57,560
我一直致力于这项工作。
I'm still working on that.

812
00:41:57,670 --> 00:41:58,670
如果我能发现结果，
And if I ever figure it out,

813
00:41:58,790 --> 00:42:00,210
我肯定会让每个人都知道。
I'll certainly let everyone know.

814
00:42:01,280 --> 00:42:05,470
是我们发明了神...
Did we invent God...

815
00:42:05,590 --> 00:42:09,010
还是神创造了我们？
or did God invent us?

816
00:42:09,120 --> 00:42:12,610
我们对人类思维的深度探索
Our expeditions into the depths of the human mind

817
00:42:12,730 --> 00:42:15,950
表明或许两种观点都是对的，
are revealing that both ideas may be correct,

818
00:42:16,060 --> 00:42:20,390
因为神与我们审视世界的角度是分不开的。
because God is inseparable from the way we see the world.

819
00:42:20,500 --> 00:42:22,490
对于神的真相的探索
The search for divine truth

820
00:42:22,600 --> 00:42:25,520
或许会使我们远离天堂
may now turn us away from the Heavens

821
00:42:25,640 --> 00:42:27,230
而朝向我们自己，
and towards the self,

822
00:42:27,340 --> 00:42:32,130
神已经编入了我们的每个纤维中，
where God is woven into every fiber of our being,

823
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:34,630
我们的信仰也可能是
and our belief could be

824
00:42:34,740 --> 00:42:38,250
使我们成为人类的关键。
the very thing that makes us human.

